  "modified": "2026-10-18T22:57:31Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: heap buffer overflow in nginx worker via map+regex\n     capture variables in script engine\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-42533.patch: backport upstream commits\n       ea47fabf55e2 (Script: simplified copy capture codes),\n       7ac67898bdfe (Script: buffer overrun protection),\n       326b17b00383 (Script: buffer overrun protection in direct script\n       usage), 78950bdcd443 (Access log: buffer overrun protection),\n       b99f804ad38a (Fixed uninitialized memory read caused by stale regex\n       captures), and 97e40e59b7b4 (Script: avoid garbage at the end of\n       the result string); add e->end pointer and\n       ngx_http_script_check_length() guard to all script copy code paths,\n       reset r->ncaptures on regex reallocation, and thread params_len /\n       headers_len through fastcgi, grpc, scgi, uwsgi upstream request\n       builders so an attacker-controlled map+regex expansion can no\n       longer overrun the assembled request or access log buffer\n     - CVE-2026-42533",
